{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Calculations","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Calculations","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Pow.Real","lean:module:QOU.KnotRegistry","lean:module:QOU.MassDerivation","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.NormNum","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Positivity","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Linarith"],"declarations":13,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Calculations.full_derivation_chain","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Calculations.full_derivation_chain","kind":"theorem","line":227,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Calculations.lean#L227-L248","doc":"**Full derivation chain**: from registry volume and CODATA mass ratio,\nwe recover the substrate parameter q within tolerance.\n\nThis theorem witnesses the complete chain:\n  KnotRegistry.figureEightEntry.volume.value\n    → h_q_squared\n    → h_q_value\n    → derived_q\n    → |derived_q - 1.1097| < 0.001\n\nKnot Atlas: <http://katlas.org/wiki/4_1> ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Calculations.derived_q_gt_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Calculations.derived_q_gt_one","kind":"theorem","line":211,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Calculations.lean#L211-L225","doc":"The derived substrate parameter satisfies q > 1, as required by the\nQOU framework (q = 1 collapses to the classical limit). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Calculations.substrate_error_bound","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Calculations.substrate_error_bound","kind":"theorem","line":154,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Calculations.lean#L154-L209","doc":"**Error bound**: The derived substrate parameter `q` is within the\n\"foolproof\" tolerance of the expected value 1.1097.\n\nSpecifically: `|derived_q - 1.1097| < 0.001`\n\nKnot Atlas: <http://katlas.org/wiki/4_1>\nRef: [codata2022] https://physics.nist.gov/cgi-bin/cuu/Value?mmusme ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Calculations.h_q_value_in_unit_interval","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Calculations.h_q_value_in_unit_interval","kind":"theorem","line":141,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Calculations.lean#L141-L152","doc":"The quantum Planck constant is in (0, 1), ensuring q > 1. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Calculations.h_q_squared_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Calculations.h_q_squared_pos","kind":"theorem","line":133,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Calculations.lean#L133-L139","doc":"The h_q² value is positive (since both Vol(4₁) and m_μ/m_e are positive). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Calculations.derived_q","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Calculations.derived_q","kind":"def","line":125,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Calculations.lean#L125-L129","doc":"The substrate parameter derived from `ℏ_q`.\n\nFrom `ℏ_q = 1 - 1/q`, we get `q = 1 / (1 - ℏ_q)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Calculations.h_q_value","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Calculations.h_q_value","kind":"def","line":119,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Calculations.lean#L119-L123","doc":"The quantum Planck constant (positive root).\n\n`ℏ_q = √(ℏ_q²) ≈ 0.09908` ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Calculations.h_q_squared","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Calculations.h_q_squared","kind":"def","line":113,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Calculations.lean#L113-L117","doc":"The squared quantum Planck constant, derived from the volume and mass ratio.\n\n`ℏ_q² = Vol(4₁) / (m_μ/m_e) ≈ 2.02988 / 206.768 ≈ 0.009817` ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Calculations.skein_mass_residue","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Calculations.skein_mass_residue","kind":"theorem","line":90,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Calculations.lean#L90-L104","doc":"The skein-deformed mass residue formula.  Given the topological mass\nconjecture, the muon-electron mass ratio equals the figure-eight\nvolume divided by the squared quantum Planck constant.\n\nThis is the central equation of the QOU mass derivation.\nRef: Manuscript Conjecture 4.25. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Calculations.neutrino_is_unknot","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Calculations.neutrino_is_unknot","kind":"theorem","line":74,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Calculations.lean#L74-L82","doc":"The registry entry for the neutrino is the unknot.\nSee `muon_is_figure_eight` for the diagnostic. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Calculations.electron_is_trefoil","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Calculations.electron_is_trefoil","kind":"theorem","line":64,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Calculations.lean#L64-L72","doc":"The registry entry for the electron is the trefoil.\nSee `muon_is_figure_eight` for the diagnostic. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Calculations.higgs_is_figure_eight","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Calculations.higgs_is_figure_eight","kind":"theorem","line":49,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Calculations.lean#L49-L62","doc":"The registry entry for the Higgs field is the figure-eight knot.\nBy construction: unfold the registry list, the find? skips\nunknotEntry (.neutrino) and trefoilEntry (.electron), then\nmatches figureEightEntry (.higgsField).\n\nNote: `.muon` has no registry entry (the muon generation-2 identity\nwould correspond to a cinquefoil entry not yet added to the registry).\n`lookupByIdentity .muon = none`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Calculations.registry_volume_eq_mass_derivation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Calculations.registry_volume_eq_mass_derivation","kind":"theorem","line":40,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Calculations.lean#L40-L47","doc":"The figure-eight knot's registry volume equals the `MassDerivation`\nvolume constant.  This ensures the mass derivation is sourced from\nthe Alexander-Briggs-indexed registry, not a free-floating constant.\n\nKnot Atlas: <http://katlas.org/wiki/4_1> ","signatureChunk":0}]}